C/ Isolates 172-OUTER.hal's whole-structure READ construct
C/ (`READ(5) ARG;`, ARG a UTIL_PARM-STRUCTURE with a VECTOR terminal
C/ among its fields) -- writes the scalar/integer/BOOLEAN fields back
C/ out individually afterward to verify READ populated every terminal's
C/ own shadow slot correctly and in the right declaration order (S1
C/ landing on the value right after V's own 3 components proves those 3
C/ were correctly consumed, even though displaying a VECTOR-shaped
C/ structure-field's own value is a separate, pre-existing gap --
C/ resolve_operand's QUAL_XPT case has no elements[]-shaped read path,
C/ only ever reads the scalar union member -- deliberately not
C/ exercised here, out of this fixture's own scope).

  TREADSTRUCT: PROGRAM;
     STRUCTURE UTIL_PARM:
        1 V VECTOR,
        1 S1 SCALAR,
        1 C INTEGER,
        1 S2 SCALAR,
        1 E BOOLEAN;
     DECLARE ARG UTIL_PARM-STRUCTURE;

     READ(5) ARG;
     WRITE(6) ARG.S1, ARG.C, ARG.S2, ARG.E;
Y %SVCI(0);
  CLOSE TREADSTRUCT;
